---
/*
 * TEMPLATE DOCUMENT — must be reviewed by a UK solicitor before launch, and the
 * ICO registration completed. See README.md ("Before you go live").
 */
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${site.company.legalName} collects, uses and protects personal data.`}
  updated="August 2026"
>
  <p class="lede">
    This policy explains what personal data {site.company.legalName} collects, why we collect it,
    and what rights you have. We are the data controller for the purposes of the UK GDPR and the
    Data Protection Act 2018.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you submit an enquiry or contact form, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name;</li>
    <li>your email address;</li>
    <li>your organisation and phone number, if you choose to provide them;</li>
    <li>the content of your message and the products you have listed;</li>
    <li>your confirmation that you accept our research-use conditions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you go on to place an order, we also collect your delivery address and the records necessary
    to process and account for that order. We do not collect or store payment card details; payments
    are handled by our payment provider, who processes them under their own privacy terms.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your enquiry list</h2>
  <p>
    The enquiry list you build while browsing is stored in your own browser using
    <code>localStorage</code>. It stays on your device and is not transmitted to us, or to anyone
    else, unless and until you submit the enquiry form. Clearing your browser data removes it.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Why we process it, and on what basis</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>To respond to your enquiry</strong> — our legitimate interest in answering people who
      contact us, or steps taken at your request prior to entering a contract.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To fulfil an order</strong> — performance of our contract with you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To meet our record-keeping obligations</strong> — compliance with a legal obligation,
      including tax and supply records.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>To send marketing</strong> — only where you have given consent, which you may withdraw
      at any time.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not lead to an order are deleted within 24 months. Order and transaction
    records are retained for six years after the end of the relevant financial year, as required by
    UK tax law. Marketing consents are held until you withdraw them.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We share personal data only with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>our website and form hosting providers, who process it on our instructions;</li>
    <li>our payment provider, for orders;</li>
    <li>our delivery carriers, to fulfil delivery;</li>
    <li>our accountants and professional advisers;</li>
    <li>public authorities, where we are legally required to do so.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it for third-party marketing.</p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers operate outside the UK. Where personal data is transferred
    overseas, we rely on UK adequacy regulations or on the International Data Transfer Agreement,
    together with appropriate supplementary safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no advertising or analytics cookies. We use browser storage for two things
    only, both strictly functional: remembering your light or dark theme preference, and holding
    your enquiry list. Neither is used to track you, and neither requires consent under the Privacy
    and Electronic Communications Regulations.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
    <li>have your data erased, where no overriding obligation requires us to keep it;</li>
    <li>restrict or object to our processing;</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
    We respond within one month.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you are unhappy with how we have handled your data, please tell us first so we can put it
    right. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, or on 0303 123 1113.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The current version is always the one published on this page, with
    the date of last revision shown above.
  </p>
</Legal>
